Id: cron011w
Severity: WARN
Category: cron
Check: check_crontabs
Fix: Take the user out of at.allow (or add them to at.deny) unless needed.
References: at(1); at.allow(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST AC-3, CM-5, CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

At is not restricted to a given user. Like cron, at lets a user have
the system run commands as them, so it has the same potential for
abuse by users or system crackers. Consider removing the user from
the allowed at list if it is not strictly needed.
